# A deployment's secrets, by process: the environment variables each one reads, and nothing else.
# Values come from your secret store, put into each process's environment by the deployment.
# Never write a value into this repository, an image, a configuration file or a log.
#
# Every key is 32 bytes of hex unless it says otherwise.

# The template runs the core as a VOS Agent (DEC-21), its keys behind the signer (F-035); ingress
# keeps its database URL, sealing key and authn key. The two marked "(in-process core only)" are for
# the fallback to the in-process core.

# --- aledgent-ingress (image aledgent-ingress) ------------------------------------------------
# Its own database and role. If the server forces TLS, the string carries sslmode=require; the
# certificate is checked against the Mozilla roots and the RDS bundle ingress embeds.
ALEDGENT_INGRESS_DATABASE_URL=postgres://aledgent_ingress:<password>@<database host>:5432/aledgent_ingress?sslmode=require
# Seals the recipients' notification secrets at rest.
ALEDGENT_INGRESS_SEALING_KEY=<32 bytes of hex>
# (in-process core only) The core's key-ring root.
# ALEDGENT_CORE_ROOT=<32 bytes of hex>
# The core link's token (F-035): ingress presents it to the core host, which lists its SHA-256 in
# ingress.json's core_link. At least 32 bytes of randomness.
ALEDGENT_CORE_LINK_TOKEN=<a random token, at least 32 bytes>
# Signs passkey challenges and session tokens (F-028). Required because ingress.json configures
# passkeys: without it ingress refuses to start. Every ingress replica takes the same value.
ALEDGENT_INGRESS_AUTHN_KEY=<32 bytes of hex>
# (in-process core only) The clerk key.
# ALEDGENT_CLERK_KEY=<32 bytes of hex>

# --- aledgent-core-host (image aledgent-core): the core as a VOS Agent (DEC-21) ---------------
# F-035: no key. The core host takes every key from the signer (below) and refuses to start if
# ALEDGENT_CORE_ROOT, ALEDGENT_CLERK_KEY, ALEDGENT_CORE_AGENT_KEY or ALEDGENT_CORE_PACKAGE_KEY is
# set. It reads one secret, from a file your secret store writes: its token for the signer,
# /etc/aledgent/core-signer.token (ingress.json's core_keys.signer.token_file).

# --- aledgent-signer (image aledgent-signer): the key boundary (F-035) -----------------------
# None: no environment variable carries a key, and none carries a Vault token. The signer reads its
# keys itself from Vault at start, logging in with AWS IAM auth under the instance role (signer.json's
# `vault` section), from the KV v1 secret its keys name:
#   keyring          the core's key-ring root. Losing it loses the book's openings: back it up as
#                    the book is.
#   clerk            the clerk key (F-017); its public half is the contract's attestation key. A
#                    canonical Ristretto scalar.
#   agent-authority  the Agent's authority key (ed25519 seed).
#   agent-package    the runtime package key (ed25519 seed).
# Each 32 bytes of hex. KMS is not required.
# The sharded profile adds one voter key per Agent (R-03, owner ruling rq-02: the root of the Agent's
# messages until F-021; Vault, not KMS), granted to the core host only and never to the relay:
#   voter-book-<n>    each book shard's (ed25519 seed)
#   voter-principals  the principals Agent's (ed25519 seed)
# Not in a single-core deployment: its one core Agent sends no message between Agents, and a field its Vault
# secret does not hold would stop the signer at start.

# --- aledgent-relay (sharded profile only) ----------------------------------------------------
# R-03, owner ruling rq-01: the relay runs as its own OS user (aledgent-relay, uid 65532) with one
# credential, admitted on the core host's relay socket (/run/aledgent/relay.sock) for stream steps
# only. No environment variable carries it: your secret store writes /etc/aledgent/relay.token at boot (mode 0400,
# owned by 65532), and the core host lists its SHA-256 and the relay's uid. The relay has no signer
# token, no Vault role and no route to the instance metadata service. Every message it carries is
# checked by its receiver against its sender's certificate, in report mode (applied, and a failure
# pages security). Across hosts it also holds its host's Noise transport key (not book key material).

# --- aledgent-settle (image aledgent-settle) ------------------------------------------------
# The lane's PASS device key and the anchor PASS device key: secp256k1 secrets. With development
# keys (settle.json's "development_keys": true) they come from the environment; otherwise they are
# the adapter's signer's, from its Vault secret (F-035; an opted-in AWS KMS key per lane
# at most), and no variable carries them.
ALEDGENT_SETTLE_LANE_0_KEY=<32 bytes of hex>
ALEDGENT_SETTLE_ANCHOR_KEY=<32 bytes of hex>
# The adapter's bearer token for ingress (its SHA-256 goes in ingress.json's tokens).
ALEDGENT_SETTLE_INGRESS_TOKEN=<a random token, at least 32 bytes>
# Its own database and role, apart from ingress's.
ALEDGENT_SETTLE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://aledgent_settle:<password>@<database host>:5432/aledgent_settle?sslmode=require

# --- opsctl exporter (image aledgent-ops) ---------------------------------------------------
# The operations principal's token: its grant is `read_signals` and nothing else.
ALEDGENT_OPS_TOKEN=<a random token, at least 32 bytes>
